More formally, given a graph $H$ which is a subgraph of the full graph $G$, we
simulate a growth sequence $H_0$, $H_1 \dots H_n$ in the following way:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $H_0 \longleftarrow H$;
  \item $V_{H_{k+1}} \longleftarrow \{\Gamma_{out}(V_{H_k}) \cup V_{H_k}\}$, with $V_x$ being the set of vertices of a graph, and $\Gamma$ being the vertex neighborhood function;
  \item $E_{H_{k+1}} \longleftarrow \{(v_1, v_2) | v_1 \in V_{H_{k+1}} \wedge v_2 \in V_{H_{k+1}} \}$, with $E_x$ being the set of edges of a graph.
